well I got a question recently about a  couple who started practicing Islam a  little bit later in their lives and they  tried to adjust their lifestyle  according to the principles of Islam and  it takes some change it takes some time  and one of the difficulties within that  relationship within that family was that  the wife had trouble wearing hijab we're  observing the modest Islamic dress and  the head covering and all the other  things that are associated with the  principle of hijab and how women should  be dressing so the husband initially was  thinking you know what I'll wait a  little while and hopefully you know try  to encourage her she maybe she just  needs some time there's a lot of family  members around none of them are  practicing like this none of them  they're gonna look at her funny they're  gonna make fun of her so he kind of you  know played it down for a while  and the sister herself would say I just  don't feel like I'm ready yet but time  passed  months passed years passed and now it's  been 10 years and the sister is still  not changing her dress she's not changed  this aspect of her lifestyle and the  husband is basically just giving up the  idea and say you know what there's  really nothing I can do I don't want to  cause more problems within the family so  let me just leave it you know I'm not  gonna not gonna push this and it's okay  you know I guess I'm just gotten used to  this fact that she dresses like this and  really not much I can do about it you  know I have to two pieces of advice you  know one for the sister you know the  wife who's actually going through this  and then a piece of advice for the  husband for the wife I would say that  you know he started practicing  practicing Islam and one of the things  that we have to keep in mind is that  when we start practicing Islam there's  gonna be help from Allah but there's  also going to be some challenges that we  encounter and remember Allah is always  there to help you as long as you're  putting in your effort you're putting in  your best effort unless got your back  and when you're making that transition  when you're making that life change into  Islam you should take it slowly you  take a little bit of time to make sure  you're adapting and you're adjusting but  you shouldn't take too long you should  make sure that whatever you're doing  you're doing it to please your Creator  you're doing it to please your Lord to  please Allah and we're not here on this  earth to please human beings so it's  very important to understand that there  is something that Allah wants from us  and when you want something from us and  it's everything he asks us to do is very  reasonable we got to look back deep down  inside our heart and saying what's  stopping me from fulfilling the  commandment that Allah has given me you  got to look into it and you say well I  don't not ready yet I need some more  time and when what will it take to get  ready will it take a few months will it  take some sign from Allah will it take  all the people around you in your family  to stop criticizing you to never give  you a funny glance or something like  that those things are never gonna happen  that's just the reality they're not  gonna happen the prophets were made fun  of the Companions were made fun of and  Muslims today there's gonna be there's  gonna be naysayers they're gonna talk  and they're gonna do these things so  once we understand this is what Allah  wants we got to make sure number one  understand that despite what we feel  despite some of the difficulties we do  it for for the cause of Allah and number  two realize that there's a wisdom behind  this and that modesty is actually the  best way in the best way to live life  this is the best thing for society  actually so when we see the wisdom  behind the command and we understand  that it is a command we shouldn't wait  too long and we should adjust ourselves  for the husband I would say there is an  aspect of trying to be soft trying to  just hold back and say I don't want to  push it I don't want to force it people  are already looking at me as being kind  of you know too tough and they're not  religious they're not practicing and  they look at me as being some kind of  extreme radical or whatever it is just  because I pray five times a day you know  what don't worry about all those things  don't worry about the naysayers and also  understand that you have a  responsibility because you are a husband  you have a responsibility over the  family the Prophet peace be upon him  said that all of you are like shepherds  and your  sponsible over your flock of sheep so in  that sense we're all we all have some  level of responsibility and a man has a  responsibility over his family just  think about it brother you know you got  if your wife goes out and she's dressing  in skin tight clothing and she likes to  wear makeup and people like that  attention but you know what that  attention is not always healthy  especially not healthy for your marriage  when you're gonna have other guys  staring at her fantasizing about her you  don't know what they might have in their  mind when they go back in the room what  they're thinking what they're doing and  they got your wife in their mind think  about that so you should have this the  sense of you know protection for your  wife you should have this love and this  care and this concern I don't want other  people disrespecting my wife by looking  at her and making her some type of sex  object or just looking at her body or  something like that so we have a  responsibility in Islam and you should  step up and fulfill that responsibility  with wisdom with gentle admonition but  also it's important you realize that  your role is not to just sit back and  wait when it comes to your wife when it  comes to your kids and say hopefully  I'll just make du'a maybe they'll change  no there's a greater responsibility and  when everyone fulfills their own  responsibility not only their families  are in check everyone in society will  fulfill their responsibilities that  society will be a better society so I  would say with wisdom  make sure you fulfill that  responsibility and really try to  motivate and encourage her and make sure  that at least if she's not gonna cover  her hair at least the clothing becomes  more and more modest over time so it  gets at least closer to what the Islamic  guidelines are when it comes to clothing
 

